{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "What Happened Last Night?"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Finding Solutions"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 13}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange information about hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le13ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Unreal Past: Impossible Situation"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you talk about the unreal past, you express things that did not happen in reality in the past. You use past tenses to talk about unreal situations. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Type 3 Conditional</span> to express conditions in the past that did not happen or to express criticism or regret with <span class=\"strong\">would have</span>, <span class=\"strong\">could have</span> or <span class=\"strong\">should have</span>.<br/> The <span class=\"strong\">Type 3 Conditional</span> is used to refer to an unreal condition that is in the past.<br/> <br/>Structure:<br/> If+ subject + Past Perfect, subject + Perfect Conditional<br/><br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">If my employees <span class=\"strong\">had studied </span> at the Blue Ribbon, they <span class=\"strong\">wouldn't have quit</span> so easily.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The condition of having studied at the Blue Ribbon is unreal. As a result, they have quite too easily."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you<span class=\"strong\"> hadn't created</span> rules, there <span class=\"strong\">would have been</span> no discipline. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I <span class=\"strong\">hadn't studied </span>there, I probably <span class=\"strong\">would have never gotten</span> into the restaurant business."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Also, If I <span class=\"strong\">hadn't gone</span> out to the west coast, I <span class=\"strong\">would have never seen</span> how beautiful California is."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I <span class=\"strong\">would have gotten</span> really good if I <span class=\"strong\">had worked </span> as a sous-chef a little longer."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If my friends<span class=\"strong\"> had lived </span> somewhere closer, I <span class=\"strong\">would have stayed </span> out there."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Colloquial Expressions about Time "}, {"type": "describer", "content": " Colloquial expressions are idioms that you use frequently, especially in spoken English. There are many expressions that refer to time in English."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Colloquial expressions about time can refer to different aspects of time. <br/>  Here are some colloquial expressions:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Lack of time:</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">pressed for time<br/> run out of time</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Have enough time:</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">lots of time<br/> take your time</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">The right time for something:</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">a great time<br/> time away</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I had a <span class=\"strong\">great time</span> there. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm sorry I'm <span class=\"strong\">pressed for time</span> today."}, {"type": "example", "content": "That's ok. We have <span class=\"strong\">lots of time</span>. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We won't <span class=\"strong\">run out of time</span>, so <span class=\"strong\">take your time</span>."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "starting to lose it"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to get mad at someone or lose your patience with them"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm starting to lose it."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le13ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when talking about the past."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to can"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to dismiss someone from their job"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have canned a supplier and had three employees quit."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le13ob06aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "appalling"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very bad"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's been an appalling week so far."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le13ob06aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hysterically"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "unable to control your feelings or behaviour because you are \u200bextremely \u200bfrightened, \u200bangry, \u200bexcited, etc."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Just not so hysterically."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le13ob06aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "unreasonable"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not fair or acceptable"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They thought my demands were unreasonable."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le13ob06aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "orderliness"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be neatly arranged and tidy"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I was just trying to establish some orderliness."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le13ob06aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Research two English idioms about time."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a powerpoint presentation. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "In your presentation, use a conversation, pictures, or other media to explain the meaning of the idiom and its use(s)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present your idioms."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research two English time idioms."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create a powerpoint presentation that creatively explains the time idiom and its uses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present my idioms in a clear and concise manner."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le13ob06re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le13ob06re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le13ob06re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Amy, I'm sorry I'm pressed for time today.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: That's ok. We have lots of time.  We won't run out of time, so take your time.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I had a terrible day at work yesterday. I really think I'm starting to lose it<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: What happened?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I had some people quit on me. I was just trying to establish some orderliness and they thought my demands were unreasonable.  So in the last two days, I have canned a supplier and had three employees quit. It's been an appalling week so far. Perhaps I'm too strict?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: If you hadn't created rules, there would have been no discipline. Had people quit before?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Sure. Just not so hysterically.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: I'm curious Vanessa. What was your background before you started this job?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I was a chef. I studied at the Blue Ribbon Institute in San Francisco. If I hadn't studied there, I probably would have never gotten into the restaurant business. Also, If I hadn't gone out to the west coast, I would have never seen how beautiful California is. Have you been?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: No.", "id": 1, "time": "50", "image": "engenn10le13ob06re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: It's gorgeous. I lived in San Francisco for nine months before I got homesick and came back to Boston.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: Are you from here?<br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: No, the U.K. I settled here after school.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: How long did you work as a sous-chef?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Six months. I would have gotten really good, if I had worked as sous-chef a little longer.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: Did you enjoy it?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I had a great time there. I really liked SanFrancisco too, but it's too far. If my friends had lived somewhere closer, I would have stayed out there.", "id": 2, "time": "64000", "image": "engenn10le13ob06re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: Have you ever wondered what your life would have been like if you had stayed in San Francisco? Have you ever wondered what your life would have be like if you had remained a sous-chef?  My point is, I wonder if managing is truly making you happy. Maybe you should take some time away?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I don't know. I guess I have been under a lot of pressure lately and that's why I'm thinking the way I am. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: Are you burning out?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Maybe. I sometimes wonder if I have worked too much this past year.\nI suppose I have burned the candle at both ends for a little long now. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: Vanessa. Do the life balance wheel for me.", "id": 3, "time": "95000", "image": "engenn10le13ob06re2img02.jpg"}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about relationships and character traits."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What do you do to kill time?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " William Penn said: \"Time is what we want most, but what we use worst.\" What do you think this means?"}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about impossible situations."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can use colloquial expressions."}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": " Talking about time!"}], "template_override": 1}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0, "selected": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1, "selected": 0}]}], "stimuli_ids": [1], "id": 1, "type": "STI", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " \nMay has been studying day and night. She is really <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">burning the candle at both ends</span>.\n"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allo